---
import JourneyMap from "../../../../components/JourneyMap.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { getJourneyOverview, getStageView } from "../../../../lib/site-data";
export function getStaticPaths() { return ["beginner", "expert"].map((mode) => ({ params: { mode } })); }
const mode = Astro.params.mode;
if (mode !== "beginner" && mode !== "expert") throw new Error("Invalid alignment mode.");
const beginner = mode === "beginner";
const journey = getJourneyOverview("encoder-decoder-alignment");
const first = getStageView(mode, "cho-2014", "encoder-decoder-alignment");
---
<BaseLayout title={`${beginner ? "Beginner" : "Expert"} path: source summaries and alignment — LLM Lineage`} description="Preview a source-scoped path through conditional sequences and encoder-decoder gates." eyebrow={`${mode} path`}>
  <div class="shell breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/journeys/encoder-decoder-alignment/">Source summaries and alignment</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">{mode}</span></div>
  <section class="journey-hero"><p class="eyebrow">{mode} path · four chapters available</p><h1>{beginner ? "Read a source. Predict a target. Inspect the difference." : "Audit the conditional model before the alignment mechanism."}</h1><p class="mt-4">{beginner ? "Use a short probability prerequisite, then predict a complete phrase score. Compare the two printed reset placements using one set of teaching inputs. Then predict which source–target pairs reversal brings closer, and explain the difference between generating and reranking translations. Then predict what changes when a new decoder state reads the same source annotations; check two cases where the context stays fixed. Finish by predicting what a local window can omit and tracing the previous attentional vector into the next input." : "Derive the target-prefix softmax and EOS-terminated likelihood; inspect every supplied logit and denominator. Reconstruct both reset placements, preserve z’s old-state convention, compare source versions and dimensions, and audit all four canonical result rows. Continue with the cited Graves cell, reversal slot arithmetic, and complete direct-generation versus rescoring evidence. Reconstruct additive source reads, normalization and signed contexts; audit appendix conflicts and the full All/No UNK comparison. Finish with current-state score shapes, source support, input feeding and complete BLEU/AER tables."}</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href={`/journeys/encoder-decoder-alignment/${mode}/cho-2014/`}>Start with Cho et al. · 2014 <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="button button--quiet" href={`/journeys/encoder-decoder-alignment/${beginner ? "expert" : "beginner"}/`}>See the {beginner ? "expert" : "beginner"} path</a></div></section>
  <section class="shell reference-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">What you need</p><ul class="mt-3">{first.objective.prerequisites.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul><p class="provenance-note mt-4">The chapter includes a conditional-sequence prerequisite and a return to the recurrent word-model chapter in the same mode. All arithmetic is synthetic; no model trains or translates.</p><a class="claim-link" href={`/journeys/recurrent-memory/${mode}/mikolov-2010/`}>Revisit recurrent word prediction</a></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Your route</p><div class="mt-3"><JourneyMap journey={journey} mode={mode} compact /></div><p class="provenance-note mt-4">Luong completes the comparison with static source operations and separate beginner/expert checkpoints. The Graves formulation prerequisite is included in Sutskever’s chapter; the handwriting-window comparison belongs to Bahdanau’s. Approximate 30/55-minute full-path estimates are planning estimates, not measured completion times.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
